,"html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-05T11:23:29Z","updated_at":"2024-12-05T11:40:08Z","body":"`SNAME` creates a static `StringName` in *each* place it is used, `SceneStringNames` is one single declaration that's reused:\r\n\r\n`SNAME`:\r\n* Static variable so evaluated exactly once, the first pass of the scope\r\n* Not shared (AFAIK the compiler can't merge these due to volatile behaviour)\r\n\r\n`SceneStringName`:\r\n* Uses a singleton\r\n* Allocated on startup\r\n* All uses of it are shared, and access should be optimized out","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2520034265/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2520247233","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100036#issuecomment-2520247233","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100036","id":2520247233,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6WN-vB","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-05T12:55:03Z","updated_at":"2024-12-05T12:55:03Z","body":"> Did you have some limit when cleaning out some cases @KoBeWi?\r\n\r\nI deleted names if they were used once or twice, so anything above would qualify. But it's different with adding new names. *Technically* adding new SceneStringNames has no downsides, but the more we have them, the more difficult is to keep track of them, which might eventually lead to inconsistencies like we had before. And opting for using a SceneStringName for everything is not very convenient. #99984 makes it easier to add new names, but it still requires major recompiling of the engine.\r\nSNAME is a middle ground between performance and convenience. You can use it easily, but it comes with some drawbacks when overused.\r\n\r\n> SceneStringName:\r\nUses a singleton\r\nAllocated on startup\r\nAll uses of it are shared, and access should be optimized out\r\n\r\nThey also prevent typos.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2520247233/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]